:: OC Percy Geebles Intro [nobr]

/* Intro */
/* Opening */
You walk up to <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and ask if he would like to play something. He gives you a wide smile before dragging you toward the playground, practically buzzing with excitement. <br>
<br>
<span style="LightSteelBlue">“Okay, <span style="DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>, we’re gonna race! But it’s not just any kind of race—it’s gonna be a super awesome obstacle race!”</span> <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> seems giddy as he explains the elaborate course: starting at the jungle gym, over some bushes, and under a row of benches. You begin to wonder just how long he’s been planning all this—it’s so detailed that you're already forgetting parts of it. <br>
<br>
After getting a bit of clarification, you both take your positions near the base of the jungle gym. You can’t help but notice the confident, almost cocky grin on <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter’s</span>face. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“Okay! On the count of three, we go! Ready? One… two… three!”</span> <br>

[Avatars: carter, eyes mad, mouth happy,]

You both dash toward the jungle gym. Luckily, you manage to make the jump and grab onto the monkey bars—the first obstacle in the long course. What follows is an intense, neck-and-neck race as you both climb, scale, and dash over and around various playground obstacles. As you begin approaching the final stretch, you manage to pull ahead. Glancing back to check how far behind <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is, you feel confident—until— <br>
<br>
<span style="Lightcoral">CRASH!</span> <br>
<br>
You slam into something hard, sending you—and what looks like snacks?—flying in all directions. For a moment, everything blurs. Your vision fills with stars from the impact.
As your head clears, you realize what—or rather, who—you hit. <br>

[Avatars: Percy, pc, percy eyes mad, tears watering, mouth sad, slight blush, pc eyes sad,tears watering, mouth normal,blush, hands hide]

A short boy with black hair, now disheveled, sits on the ground looking dazed. He’s wearing short shorts, and you spot a small scrape on his knee. Surrounding him is an avalanche of snacks, all likely from the school vending machines, and far more than any one person could eat alone. It finally clicks that you just barreled straight into him—and you should probably apologize. But he speaks first. <br>
<br>
<span style="LightSteelBlue">“Ow! Ugh, what’s wrong with you!? Why don’t you watch where you’re going next time!”</span> he shouts, pushing himself up and brushing off his clothes. He winces when he moves his injured leg. Then his eyes go wide as he notices the mess around him. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“Ah, damn it! Not the snacks—he’s gonna kill me!”</span> He drops to his knees, letting out another pained hiss as he starts gathering the scattered food. After a moment, he shoots a scornful look your way. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“Well, don’t just stand there—help me!”</span> However, his voice didnt sound angry, but rather it was full of desperation and fear <br>
<br>
Without a word, you drop down and start helping him collect the snacks and drinks. It only takes a few seconds, but the two of you manage to gather everything. You hand him the last of it. His tone softens as he accepts the pile from you, looking a bit sad now. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“I, um… I’m sorry for yelling earlier. I didn’t even ask if you’re okay.”</span> You shake your head and let him know that you should be the one apologizing since it's your fault for not paying attention. <br>
<br>
Before anything else can be said, <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> finally catches up, panting as he rushes to your side. His eyes scan you with worry. “<span style="DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span> <span style="LightSteelBlue">, are you okay!? I saw the crash from back there—it looked painful. You could’ve—</span> <span style="DarkTurquoise">Percy</span>?” <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter’s</span>sentence cuts off as his eyes lock onto the boy you collided with. Judging by the reaction, you guess that must be the boy's name. <br>
<br>
The air shifts. You find yourself suddenly tense, caught between the two boys. <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> starts to blush slightly and gives a nervous smile, while <span style="DarkTurquoise">Percy</span> looks thoroughly unimpressed and annoyed. <br>

[Avatars:carter, pc, percy, carter eyes sad, mouth happy, blush slight, hands bound, pc mouth sad, blush slight, hands hide, percy eyes tired, tears watering, mouth sad]

He turns his gaze toward you. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“You should be careful with him. That bad luck of his tends to rub off. But I guess  now the crash makes sense.”</span> With a slight scoff, he turns away from <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> —only to flinch at the sound of someone calling his name from across the courtyard. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“I... I gotta go. See you around, <span style="DarkTurquoise">$Player.Name</span>.” <br>
<br>
You blink as <span style="DarkTurquoise">Percy</span> jogs off toward a somewhat large group of students. You recognize a few of them as bullies who usually hang around Michael. They don’t seem too friendly toward <span style="DarkTurquoise">Percy</span> . You can’t hear everything they say, but it’s clear he’s being scolded by one of the bigger-looking kids, most likely the leader of the little group, the snacks are taken from him. He doesn’t get to keep a single one. <br>
<br>
You turn to <span style="DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> and ask what that was about. He quickly shakes his head. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“It was nothing. Just an... um, old friend.”</span> He forces a smile and gestures back toward the playground. <span style="LightSteelBlue">“Come on, we can still finish the race. Let’s just continue from here.”</span> You let out a quiet sigh and nod, the two of you taking off again to finish the final leg of the course. <br>

